1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,601
ClearCheckout helps people navigate a checkout at their own
pace. This is the real public app. Local

2
00:00:03,601 --> 00:00:07,203
label repair and optional Meta assistance keep the shopper in
control. All payments in this demo are

3
00:00:07,203 --> 00:00:10,804
simulated.

4
00:00:11,304 --> 00:00:15,771
A synthetic demo account starts with personal reading
preferences. No payment details are requested.

5
00:00:15,771 --> 00:00:20,237
Here we choose large text, then save our preferences to our
own space.

6
00:00:20,737 --> 00:00:24,316
The dashboard brings the demo store and saved preferences
together. This prototype demonstrates a

7
00:00:24,316 --> 00:00:27,895
focused shopping journey. It does not claim support for every
store, or completed testing with

8
00:00:27,895 --> 00:00:31,475
screen reader users.

9
00:00:31,975 --> 00:00:35,866
The clarity panel scans demo controls and repairs reliable
labels locally. The previously unnamed

10
00:00:35,866 --> 00:00:39,757
cart button now has a useful name. Unknown controls still need
human judgment. Field values are not

11
00:00:39,757 --> 00:00:43,649
uploaded by this scan.

12
00:00:44,149 --> 00:00:47,996
Muse Spark explains an approved order summary. The screen
discloses that Contributor prompts and

13
00:00:47,996 --> 00:00:51,844
responses may be used for training. I explicitly approve this
request. The trusted app total remains

14
00:00:51,844 --> 00:00:55,691
the source to verify.

15
00:00:56,191 --> 00:01:00,081
Muse Spark explains the items, delivery and next step in plain
language. The app sends prices

16
00:01:00,081 --> 00:01:03,971
already formatted in dollars. The trusted total remains forty
two dollars. AI guidance cannot change

17
00:01:03,971 --> 00:01:07,860
or confirm the order.

18
00:01:08,360 --> 00:01:12,458
Voice navigation uses Muse Voice Transcribe. This nonprivate
synthetic recording says, go to cart.

19
00:01:12,458 --> 00:01:16,555
Selecting a file stays local until I choose Send audio to
Meta. A transcript must be reviewed before

20
00:01:16,555 --> 00:01:20,652
applying a supported command.

21
00:01:21,152 --> 00:01:26,304
The real transcript is ready for review. I apply go to cart,
which moves navigation to the cart.

22
00:01:26,304 --> 00:01:31,456
Voice commands cannot edit quantities or confirm payment. The
final decision remains manual.

23
00:01:31,956 --> 00:01:37,155
Muse Image supplies a saved illustrative scene, not a product
photograph. I select the mug and

24
00:01:37,155 --> 00:01:42,353
explicitly request SAM localization. No checkout fields or
page images are sent for this step.

25
00:01:42,853 --> 00:01:46,692
SAM returns actual highlighted regions and a magnified view.
This helps inspect the illustration. A

26
00:01:46,692 --> 00:01:50,531
box is an object region, not arbitrary checkout understanding,
and SAM does not verify the product

27
00:01:50,531 --> 00:01:54,370
details.

28
00:01:54,870 --> 00:01:58,664
Finally, I review the items, delivery and total. I type the
exact phrase shown by the app, then

29
00:01:58,664 --> 00:02:02,459
press Confirm simulated payment myself. Neither the
explanation nor voice navigation can perform

30
00:02:02,459 --> 00:02:06,253
this confirmation.

31
00:02:06,753 --> 00:02:10,877
The demo is complete. No money moved and no real order was
placed. ClearCheckout combines local

32
00:02:10,877 --> 00:02:15,002
control repair, plain language guidance, reviewed voice
navigation and visual exploration, with a

33
00:02:15,002 --> 00:02:19,126
deliberate human confirmation at the end.
